System calls used:
fork()	  Creates a child process
getpid()	  Returns the Process ID (PID)
getppid()	  Returns the Parent Process ID (PPID)

Process States:
Ready State:
The process is prepared to execute and is waiting for CPU time from the scheduler.
Running State:
The process is currently being executed by the CPU.
Waiting State:
The process is waiting for an event or resource. For example, a parent process calling wait() enters a waiting state until its child process finishes.
Terminated State:
The process has completed its execution and exits the system.

Tools used :
ps – displays information about currently running processes and their states.
top – provides real-time information about processes and their resource usage.
/proc – provides detailed information about processes through the /proc/PID/ directory.
